## What happened

Step 1 — prediction committed alone (d78cc680), before opening src/prompt_retry.rs. Three hypotheses built only from callers (prompt.rs, watch.rs, tool_wrappers.rs, commands_retry.rs) and shared constants (providers.rs), each with the literal command that would settle it.

Step 2 — graded: 0 hit / 1 partial / 2 miss.

| | verdict | why |
|---|---|---|
| h1 provider-specific key guidance hardcoded to Anthropic | miss | Already reads cli::provider_api_key_env (#590), with three tests on it — a zero-information slot by my own rule |
| h2 tool_recovery_hint drifted behind BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES | partial | Class right (shared_state/todo/ask_user have no arm) — but sub_agent, the other instance I named, has arms in both branches |
| h3 uncapped tool-error interpolation | miss | safe_truncate(err, 200) / (tool_error, 300), with 200/201 boundary tests |

Two of my three bets were the same bet twice: *"error-recovery code is careless." It isn't — it's been repaired a lot. The axis I was wrong on is **correction state**: my archive priors say how a genre is written*, never how much it has since been fixed.

Step 3 — the fix came from the neighbours of a losing bet. Grading h1 meant reading diagnose_api_error's arms, where four of five branches decided by bare substring match on three-digit status codes. prompt is too long: 402134 tokens contains 402 — so a context overflow was diagnosed as exhausted credits, telling the user "retrying won't help" when the real remedy is /compact. A confident wrong diagnosis in error-recovery code is worse than none, because the user acts on it.

contains_status_code now requires a digit boundary, not a word boundary — HTTP 401, status=401, (401) still fire; 402134, 4290ms, 14012 no longer do. Pinned at the emission point (the string the caller receives), including the near-miss guard that a real 401 still reaches the auth branch.

Two things I'd flag honestly: the helper failed clippy -D dead-code on its first edit — my own "no definition without its consumer" rule catching me mid-act. And h2 was deliberately not fixed: the catch-all hint is degraded-but-true, so arms there would be cargo-culting.

cargo build, clippy -D warnings, cargo test (5045 passed) all green — including tests/blind_round_grades.rs, which would have reverted this whole task had the grade not landed.
